---
title: Missy's "Make Me Move" Smoothie (Clone)
servings: 1
source: Reconstructed from Missy's Bakehouse (Swansea) menu description and ingredient photo
tags:
  - smoothie
  - drinks
  - clone recipe
---

-- ===Base smoothie=== -- Chill the yoghurt and coconut drink beforehand, and use frozen (not fresh) berries.

Add @Koko unsweetened coconut drink{100%ml}, @vanilla Greek yoghurt{150%g}, @honey{15%g}, @frozen strawberries{100%g} and @frozen blueberries{70%g} to a #blender{}, in that order -- liquid first, then yoghurt, then honey, then berries, so the blades catch properly. Add @vanilla extract{1/4%tsp}, @blue spirulina{1/2%tsp} -- roughly 1g -- and @sea moss{} -- use the amount labelled as a single serving on your specific product rather than defaulting to a tablespoon, since sea moss gel/powder potency varies a lot by brand -- at the same time.

-- ===Optional protein + creatine version=== -- Source notes the protein powder may itself be contributing to sweetness/thickness, so it's worth blending this as a separate first test rather than assuming it's a simple addition.

For a protein version, also add @vanilla whey protein{25%g} and @creatine monohydrate{5%g} to the base ingredients above before blending.

-- ===Blend=== -- 35-45 second range in source, resolved to a midpoint.

Blend on high for ~blending{40%seconds}, stopping to scrape down the sides of the #blender{} if necessary.

-- ===Check and adjust consistency=== -- Aim for a consistency that pours slowly but doesn't need eating with a spoon. Avoid fixing consistency with ice, as it dilutes the berry flavour.

If too thick, add extra @Koko unsweetened coconut drink{10%ml} at a time. If too thin, add extra @frozen strawberries{35%g} at a time -- 30-40g range resolved to midpoint.

-- ===Taste and adjust=== -- Optional fine-tuning based on source guidance, applied in this order.

If too sour, add extra @honey{5%g}.
If too blueberry-heavy, add extra @frozen strawberries{25%g}.
If not creamy enough, add extra @vanilla Greek yoghurt{30%g}.
If too thick, add extra @Koko unsweetened coconut drink{15%ml} -- 10-20ml range resolved to midpoint.
If too thin, add extra @frozen strawberries{40%g} -- 30-50g range resolved to midpoint.
If not vanilla-y enough, add a further @vanilla extract{1/8%tsp}.
If too coconutty, switch to (or confirm) the unsweetened Koko variant and reduce the total coconut drink to around 85%ml.

-- Note: banana is deliberately excluded -- it's absent from both the menu description and the ingredient photo, and would over-thicken/over-sweeten the drink, masking the strawberry and blueberry flavour.
